<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xml:lang="en"
      xmlns:tal="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/tal"
      xmlns:metal="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/metal"
      xmlns:i18n="http://xml.zope.org/namespaces/i18n"
      lang="en"
      metal:use-macro="context/@@main_template/macros/master"
      i18n:domain="plone">
<body>

<!--
  z3c.jbot override of Products.CMFPlone/browser/login/templates/pwreset_form.pt
  (Plone 6.2). Shipped by medialog.docenttheme; active only under
  IMedialogDocentthemeLayer.

  Purpose: when the "set your password" link an administrator sends to a new
  member carries the account in its ?userid= query parameter, prefill the
  "My user name is" field with that value and lock it (readonly), so the
  invitee does not have to know / retype their own username.

  Only the userid/email field differs from upstream.

  It used to read request/userid and go readonly when that was present. That
  left the self-service "forgot password" flow with an EMPTY box, because
  those links carry no ?userid= (see PasswordResetToolView.construct_url) -
  and an empty box named "userid" is exactly what a browser password manager
  fills, with whatever login is saved for the site. People arrived here with
  "admin" in the field. readonly does not stop autofill.

  The token in the URL already identifies the account, so the name now comes
  from @@docent-pwreset-userid (DocentIMS.ActionItems) and renders as a
  hidden input plus plain text - autofill cannot touch a hidden input. Where
  there is no usable token the box stays visible and editable, since the
  visitor then has to identify themselves.

  NOTE: DocentIMS.ActionItems ships a jbot override of this same Plone
  template. Both are layer-gated and only one can win; on a themed project
  site it is this one. Keep the two in step - a fix applied to only one of
  them renders to nothing, which is exactly how the autofill bug survived
  three rounds of "fixes".
-->

<metal:custom_title fill-slot="content-title">
        <h1 class="documentFirstHeading"
            i18n:translate="heading_reset_password">Set your password</h1>
</metal:custom_title>

<metal:custom_desc fill-slot="content-description">
        <div class="documentDescription"
           i18n:translate="description_reset_password">
            Please fill out the form below to set your password.
        </div>
</metal:custom_desc>

<metal:content-core fill-slot="content-core">
<metal:content-core define-macro="content-core" tal:define="errors view/getErrors">

            <form class="enableAutoFocus"
                  name="pwreset_action"
                  method="post"
                  tal:attributes="action request/getURL">
                <fieldset>
                    <legend i18n:translate="legend_new_password">New Password</legend>
                    <input type="hidden"
                           name="randomstring"
                           value=""
                           tal:attributes="value options/randomstring | request/randomstring | nothing" />

                    <div class="mb-3 field"
                         tal:define="error errors/userid | nothing;
                                     use_email_as_login python:context.portal_registry['plone.use_email_as_login'];
                                     lookup python:context.restrictedTraverse('@@docent-pwreset-userid', None);
                                     known_userid python:lookup and lookup() or '';
                                     prefill python:known_userid or request.get('userid', '');"
                         tal:attributes="class python:error and 'mb-3 field error' or 'mb-3 field'"
                         tal:condition="here/portal_password_reset/checkUser | nothing">

                      <label class="form-label" for="userid"
                             tal:condition="not:use_email_as_login"
                             i18n:translate="label_my_user_name_is">My user name is</label>
                      <label class="form-label required" for="userid"
                             tal:condition="use_email_as_login"
                             i18n:translate="label_my_email_address_is">My email address is</label>

                      <!-- Known account: submit it hidden and show it as
                           text. A hidden input is the one thing a password
                           manager will not overwrite; a readonly text input
                           is not - that is how "admin" got in. -->
                      <tal:known tal:condition="prefill">
                        <input type="hidden" name="userid" id="userid"
                               tal:attributes="value prefill" />
                        <p class="form-control-plaintext" id="userid-display"
                           tal:content="prefill">someone</p>
                      </tal:known>

                      <tal:unknown tal:condition="not:prefill">
                        <input class="form-control"
                            name="userid"
                            required="required"
                            id="userid"
                            autocomplete="off"
                            value="" />
                      </tal:unknown>

                      <div tal:content="error" class="invalid-feedback">Validation error output</div>

                      <small class="formHelp text-muted"
                             tal:condition="not:use_email_as_login"
                             i18n:translate="help_userid">
                          Enter your user name for verification.
                      </small>
                      <small class="formHelp text-muted"
                             tal:condition="use_email_as_login"
                             i18n:translate="help_verify_email">
                          Enter your email address for verification.
                      </small>

                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-3 field"
                         tal:define="error errors/password | nothing;"
                         tal:attributes="class python:error and 'mb-3 field error' or 'mb-3 field'">

                        <label class="form-label required" for="password"
                               i18n:translate="label_new_password">New password</label>

                        <input class="form-control"
                            type="password"
                            id="password"
                            name="password"
                            required="required"
                            size="10" />

                        <div tal:content="error" class="invalid-feedback">Validation error output</div>

                        <small class="formHelp text-muted"
                            i18n:translate="help_new_password">
                            Enter your new password.
                        </small>

                    </div>

                    <div class="mb-3 field"
                         tal:define="error errors/password | nothing;"
                         tal:attributes="class python:error and 'mb-3 field error' or 'mb-3 field'">

                        <label class="form-label required" for="password2"
                        i18n:translate="label_confirm_password">Confirm password</label>

                        <input class="form-control"
                            type="password"
                            id="password2"
                            name="password2"
                            required="required"
                            size="10"
                            />

                        <div tal:content="error" class="invalid-feedback">Validation error output</div>

                        <small class="formHelp text-muted" i18n:translate="help_confirm_password">
                            Re-enter the password. Make sure the passwords are identical.
                        </small>

                    </div>

                    <div>
                        <div class="label">&nbsp;</div>

                        <div class="mb-3 field">
                            <button class="btn btn-primary"
                                type="submit"
                                value="Set my password"
                                i18n:attributes="value">
                                <span i18n:translate="">Set my password</span>
                            </button>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <input type="hidden" name="form.submitted" value="1" />
                </fieldset>
            </form>

</metal:content-core>
</metal:content-core>

</body>
</html>
